ugust, but the remaining gap is large", "Polymarket prices Warmington near 5 percent"], "rationale": "Every recent survey shows Ayotte ahead, from four points at UNH to eleven in the Times/Siena poll, and raters call the race Likely Republican. The tightening since August is real, but Warmington still faces a large deficit with under a month to go.", "watch": "A follow-up University of New Hampshire or Saint Anselm poll showing the gap under five points would move the race toward Lean R.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Kelly Ayotte (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Governor Kelly Ayotte seeks a second term against Democrat Cinde Warmington in a state that narrowly favored Democrats at the presidential level. Every recent poll shows Ayotte ahead: Saint Anselm College had her up seven in late September, the New York Times/Siena survey eleven, and the University of New Hampshire four. Ratings from national analysts cluster at Likely Republican, with one rating the race Safe Republican and two calling it Lean Republican. Prediction markets give Warmington roughly a five percent chance.\n\nThe race has narrowed since August, when Ayotte led by ten or eleven points, and Eric Holder's endorsement of Warmington reflects Democratic engagement. But the remaining gap is substantial with little time left, and police leaders criticizing Warmington over a death-penalty case have shaped recent coverage. Ayotte's incumbency and steady approval keep her favored, though New Hampshire's Democratic lean and a favorable midterm environment leave room for a closer finish.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0651, "margin": -8.09}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0566, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0654, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0669, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0672, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0698, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0784, "